          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE: TAKING A SAMPLE FROM A COLLECTION OF SINE WAVES\n\nIn this example we are generating a collection of 50 sine waves by using the Linear node in conjunction with the Sine node.\nNext we take a sample from these 50 values with the Span node.\nThe Span node will always read from position 0, but we can change the size at will.\nTry moving the slider and see what happens.\n\nEven though we might only be reading 5 values from the sine wave collection, we still see 50 circles at all time.\nThis is because the Linear node that goes into the Float2 node is set to 50.\nIf the collection from the Span is smaller than 50, Wire will automatically repeat it."
          }
        },
